You said: how is the floppy pen when you wiggle it loosely in between your fingers and a toy bow with a suction cup with a string thats not wound tight and the grip of the pen by the hand related
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 how is the floppy pen when you wiggle it loosely in between your fingers and a toy bow with a suction cup with a string thats not wound tight and the grip of the pen by the hand related

\par 09:31
\par These three phenomena are related through }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 standing wave mechanics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 , }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 node/antinode physics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 , and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 rotational pivots}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 .
\par Here is exactly how these three specific examples connect:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 1. The Floppy Pen Illusion
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls1\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 The Action:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
 You pinch a rigid pen loosely at about one-third of its length and waggle your hand up and down.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 The Physics:}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029  Your fingers act as a loose, flexible pivot point (a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 node}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
 of minimal displacement). The ends of the pen whip back and forth dynamically (the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 antinodes}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
). Because the human eye cannot process the rapid changes in direction at the tips, your brain smooths out the motion. This creates the optical illusion that the rigid plastic is bending like rubber. [}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinmagic.com/p/S5188"}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 {\*\datafield }}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cs40\ul\cf2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 1}}}\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\endnhere\sectlinegrid360\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 ]
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 2. The Toy Bow and Suction Cup String
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls2\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 The Action:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029  
A loose, unwound string is attached to a toy bow. When the bow moves or the string is plucked, it flops around lazily.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 The Physics:}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
 The two ends of the string tied to the bow are fixed anchor points (nodes). Because the string is not wound tight, it lacks tension. Low tension dramatically slows down the speed of the wave traveling through the string. This makes the string oscillate i
n large, slow, highly visible waves with maximum displacement in the center (the antinode).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 3. The Grip of the Pen
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls3\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 The Action:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
 Holding the pen loosely between your fingers rather than gripping it tightly. [}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 HYPERLINK "https://www.spielwarenmesse.de/en/mag/toy-lab/pain-free-writing/"}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 {\*\datafield }}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs40\ul\cf2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 1}}}\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\endnhere\sectlinegrid360\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj {
