\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029  This grip acts as the bridge between the physics of the string and the pen.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \hich\af2\dbch\af31506\loch\f2 o\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li1440\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx1440\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls3\ilvl1\adjustright\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
If you grip the pen tightly, your hand forces the entire pen to match your hand's exact movement, killing any independent vibration.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning2\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \hich\af2\dbch\af31506\loch\f2 o\tab}By holding it loosely, you create a low-resistance, pivotable }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 boundary condition}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 \emdash 
much like the loose string. This allows the pen to pivot freely, lag behind your hand's motion, and execute the harmonic oscillations required to create the "floppy" optical illusion.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9011029 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 The Unified Connection
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 All three rely on }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 low-restricting pivot points}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 
 that allow an object to flex or rotate away from its resting state, creating visible wave-like oscillations (antinodes) around a central point of control (the node).
