\insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029  When your photoreceptors (specifically the rods and cones in your peripheral vision) receive the exact same unchanging light levels for too long, they stop firing signals to your brain. [}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9011029\charrsid9011029 HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/UofGlasgow/posts/for-our-next-trick-the-fading-picture-keep-your-gaze-focused-on-the-black-cross-/2017975904888781/"}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
